# Furious Forebear: ruling - "If Furious Forebear leaves your graveyard before its ability resolves, it won't be returned to your
# hand even if you pay {1}{W}." Bot2's Bolt kills the Forebear (nothing triggers: it wasn't in the graveyard), a second Bolt kills
# Bot1's Memnite and the ability triggers from the graveyard; in response Bot2's Tormod's Crypt exiles Bot1's graveyard. The
# ability still asks for {1}{W}, and Bot1 pays (the Plains and Mox Jet), but the Forebear in exile is a new object (CR 400.7)
# and stays there.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Furious Forebear
Memnite
Plains
Plains
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Lightning Bolt
Lightning Bolt
Tormod's Crypt
Island x20

